      "cat-harness:section": "4. Native Rust Crate Workspaces (`crates/`) & Fast Witnessed-Value Evaluators",
      "prov:value": "Owner directive, 2026-11-28: standardise top-level `crates/` Cargo workspaces across scientific folios (`folio-assistant-sci` and paper folios), separating domain-agnostic core computer-algebra crates (`0` C-FFI, reusable across `folio-assistant-sci` without domain/application clutter) from high-precision (`MPFR`) evaluation and solver layers (`Clarabel.rs` etc.) and fast witnessed-value evaluators (`qou-values`-style high-precision `.rs` observable/witness evaluators) and application probes built on top; declare `\"id\": \"crates\"` (`graphTypologies: [\"code\"]`) in `<instance>.json` and register every crate CLI and evaluator as a validated `tool-definition/v1` node in `tools/` (`check:tools`), following `two-phase-move` when migrating legacy paths.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-28",
        "owner"
      ],
